[[12292,4747,"There was an apparent lack of training for the staff at Hurst Hall in the appropriate use of calling either 999 or 111","lack of training in emergency call procedures",""],[12293,4747,"The staff did not know how to arrange for the attendance of a GP fora resident who was not yet fully registered with a local GP","ignorance of temporary GP registration process",""],[12294,4747,"The level and quality of observation of the residents were very poor and did not include even some of the most basic issues such as whether the patient was warm, thirsty etc","inadequate resident observation",""],[12295,4747,"There seemed to be a complete lack of understanding about the legal requirement for prompt reporting of such matters as occurred in this case to the Care Quality Commission","failure to report to CQC",""],[12296,4747,"When a local GP was visiting another patient at the Home, the staff seemed unaware that they could and should have asked that doctor to look at this patient/resident","staff fail to request GP assessment",""],[12297,4747,"There was a complete failure to maintain food and hydration records","missing nutrition and hydration documentation",""]]